# Agent scripts location

When adding one-off or task scripts (analysis, migration helpers, temporary generators, peeks), put them under:

```
scripts/tasks/
```

Use other `scripts/` subfolders when they fit:

- `scripts/scratch/` — temporary dumps (`_tmp_*`), safe to delete
- `scripts/deploy/` — deploy/setup `.ps1` / `.bat` (root shims may call these)
- `scripts/archive/` — old demos, extracted assets, parked jars

## Do not

- Drop new helper `.py` / `.ps1` in the repo root
- Park scratch next to release entrypoints in `tools/` (use `scripts/scratch/`)

## Keep in `tools/`

Release and day-to-day pipeline only, e.g. `publish_client_pack.py`, `sync_lodestone_mods.py`, `upload_launcher_release.py`, `upload_pack_release.py`, `generate_site.py`, `deploy_to_cloudflare.py`, `pack_launcher_zip.py`.

Domain helpers live in `tools/{quests,patches,portal,assets,server_setup,launcher_tests}/`. Thin shims may exist at `tools/<name>.py` for CI/old paths.
